# Generated by theme/blackwall-theme, but committed anyway: hyprland.conf
# `source`s colors.conf and kitty.conf `include`s colors.conf, so a fresh clone
# that lacks them starts with a broken config rather than an unstyled one. They
# are regenerated on every wallpaper change; the committed copy is just a
# working default. The blanket `colors.*` rule above would otherwise catch both.
!hypr/configs/colors.conf
!kitty/colors.conf

# the installer build output; built on the target machine by ./install
installer/target/

# fish rewrites this on every `set -U`, so it collects machine state and
# secrets (a MODEL_API_KEY was sitting in the tracked copy). The intentional
# exports are seeded by the installer step `fish-universals` instead.
fish/fish_variables*

# Written per machine by the installer (modifier key, monitors, GPU, extra
# binds). hypr/lua/machine.lua.example is the tracked template.
hypr/lua/machine.lua

